{title: Auld Lang Syne}
{composer: Robert Burns}
{key: C}
{genre: Folk}
{language: English}

{section: Verse 1}
Should [C]auld acquaintance [Am]be forgot
And [F]never brought to [G]mind
Should [C]auld acquaintance [Am]be forgot
And [F]auld [G]lang [C]syne

{section: Chorus}
For [C]auld lang [Am]syne my dear
For [F]auld lang [G]syne
We'll [C]take a cup of [Am]kindness yet
For [F]auld [G]lang [C]syne

{section: Verse 2}
And [C]surely you'll buy [Am]your pint cup
And [F]surely I'll buy [G]mine
And [C]we'll take a cup of [Am]kindness yet
For [F]auld [G]lang [C]syne

{section: Chorus}
